Peer Review Dashboard – Randomized Encounter Selection Overview

This SQL script powers the Peer Review Dashboard by selecting randomized encounters per provider on a quarterly basis. It is designed to streamline peer review processes and support automation by pulling 8 distinct, 
randomly selected patient encounters per provider per quarter, excluding non-billable or incomplete visits.

Key Logic
Randomization: Each run of the script refreshes the patient list using NEWID() to generate a new randomized order of eligible visits.
Quarterly Grouping: Encounters are grouped by year and quarter for time-based segmentation.
Data Scope: The script only includes data from the previous 12 months, filtering by encounter timestamp.

Visit Criteria: 
Only completed and billable visits are included (billable_ind = 'Y').
Non-encounters are excluded using timestamp and billing indicators.
Only encounters with a valid provider (provider_id present) are included.

Enhancements & Features:
Random Sampling: Selects 8 visits per provider, per quarter across various service lines: Behavioral Health (BH), Mental Health (MH), Nutrition, and Primary Care

Vaccination Indicator: 
A Vaccine field flags visits related to vaccinations by checking diagnosis descriptions.

Rolling Time Frame:
Looks at encounters in the past year, segmented by quarter.

Automation Ready:
Built to support automated workflows (e.g. QI can pull/send lists directly to the providers).

Expanded Data Fields:
Output includes patient and visit details: Patient number, full name, DOB, encounter date/time, Billable status, visit type, specialty, provider name, location name

Data Integrity:
Only completed encounters are included, based on encounter ID and billing status.

Exclusions:
Case Management visits are excluded (no associated provider ID).

======================================================
Peer Review Dashboard: Randomized Encounter Selection
Description:
Selects 8 random, billable, completed patient visits 
per provider per quarter from the past 12 months.
======================================================

SELECT * 
FROM (
    SELECT        
        -- Patient and Provider Info
        p.person_nbr AS [Patient Number],
        pm.last_name AS [Provider Last Name],

        -- Quarterly Grouping
        DATEPART(YEAR, pe.enc_timestamp) AS [Encounter Year],
        DATEPART(QUARTER, pe.enc_timestamp) AS [Encounter Quarter],
        CONCAT('Q', DATEPART(QUARTER, pe.enc_timestamp), ' ', DATEPART(YEAR, pe.enc_timestamp)) AS [Quarterly Date],

        -- Encounter Details
        MIN(CAST(pe.enc_timestamp AS date)) AS [Encounter Date],
        FORMAT(MIN(pe.enc_timestamp), 'h:mm tt') AS [Encounter Time],

        -- Visit & Provider Metadata
        MAX(pe.billable_ind) AS [Billed?],
        MAX(sm.description) AS [Provider Specialty],
        MAX(m.specialty) AS [Visit Specialty],
        MAX(m.Visit_type) AS [Visit Type],
        MAX(dx.[Vaccine]) AS [Vaccine],

        -- Random Row Number within Provider + Quarter
        ROW_NUMBER() OVER (
            PARTITION BY pm.provider_id, 
                         DATEPART(YEAR, pe.enc_timestamp), 
                         DATEPART(QUARTER, pe.enc_timestamp)
            ORDER BY NEWID()
        ) AS [Random Pt]

    FROM Patient_encounter pe

    -- Joins
    LEFT JOIN Person p ON pe.person_id = p.person_id
    LEFT JOIN Location_mstr lm ON pe.location_id = lm.location_id
    LEFT JOIN Provider_mstr pm ON pe.rendering_provider_id = pm.provider_id
    LEFT JOIN provider_practice_mstr ppm ON pe.rendering_provider_id = ppm.provider_id
    LEFT JOIN specialty_mstr sm ON ppm.specialty_code = sm.specialty_code
    LEFT JOIN master_im_ m ON pe.enc_id = m.enc_id

    -- Join Vaccine Diagnosis (Subquery)
    LEFT JOIN (
        SELECT 
            pd.person_id, 
            pd.description AS [Vaccine]
        FROM patient_diagnosis pd
        WHERE pd.description LIKE '%vaccine%'
    ) AS dx ON pe.person_id = dx.person_id

    -- Filters
    WHERE pe.enc_timestamp >= DATEADD(YEAR, -1, GETDATE())                --> Past year only
      AND CAST(pe.enc_timestamp AS time) <> '00:00:00'                    --> Exclude zero-time encounters
      AND pe.billable_ind = 'Y'                                           --> Only billable visits
      AND pm.first_name IS NOT NULL AND pm.last_name IS NOT NULL          --> Valid provider
      AND pe.location_id IN (                                             --> Approved locations
            '9D971E61-2B5A-4504-9016-7FD863790EE2', 
            'A97BF74E-A822-468E-871E-197FD3C21314', 
            'E6764687-D771-4420-9D04-92370E8BA245', 
            'D8CC9783-E862-49A2-A82F-8983BAEA23FC', 
            '58D75176-5578-4DCF-BDBE-AFFDCEB0D77E', 
            '00D2BE2A-7960-44CA-A7EF-24AFC233A761'
        )

    -- Group by for randomization and aggregation
    GROUP BY 
        p.person_id, p.person_nbr, p.first_name, p.last_name, p.date_of_birth,
        lm.location_name, pm.first_name, pm.last_name, pm.provider_id,        
        DATEPART(YEAR, pe.enc_timestamp), 
        DATEPART(QUARTER, pe.enc_timestamp)
) AS Enclist

-- Final Filter: Only 8 Random Patients Per Provider Per Quarter
WHERE [Random Pt] <= 8

-- Order Output
ORDER BY [Provider Last Name], [Quarterly Date], [Random Pt];




